arian services. Consequently, the ETT coverage focuses on the main urban centers and surrounding villages for each assessed district. The data is collected through Key Informant Interviews (KIIs) at the location level, from Saturday to Wednesday, every week. It includes information on new arrivals, numbers and demographic of IDPs, reasons for displacement, intentions, humanitarian assistance and priority needs among others. \n\nTo facilitate the joint analysis of the CCCM (Camp Coordination and Camp Management) Cluster\u2019s New Arrivals Tracker (NAT) and ETT data, the assistance and needs indicators are identical in both tools._6",
